# ---- Supabase: authentication only ----
# Supabase provides sign-in and nothing else. Every planner row (tasks, habits,
# goals, blocks, settings, notifications) is stored on the device in IndexedDB
# via `src/data/local-db.ts`; nothing planner-related is ever sent to Supabase.
# There is therefore no planner schema to apply: the files in
# `supabase/migrations/` are the reference the local schema was derived from,
# not something the app runs. Auth needs only these two values.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key-here
VITE_APP_URL=http://localhost:5173

# ---- Server-side only (no VITE_ prefix, so it never reaches the browser) ----
# Required for the planning assistant. Locally: put it in .env. In production:
# set it in your host's environment variables (e.g. Vercel project settings).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# All optional. The assistant only ever uses 100% free models: the model below
# is honoured only while OpenRouter still reports it as free, and the free
# router (openrouter/free) is always available as a fallback.
OPENROUTER_MODEL=openrouter/free
OPENROUTER_MAX_TOKENS=800
OPENROUTER_TEMPERATURE=0.4
# OPENROUTER_SYSTEM_PROMPT=

# ---- AI endpoint access control ----
# /api/ai/* is authenticated: the browser sends the signed-in member's Supabase
# access token, and the server validates it against Supabase before spending any
# OpenRouter quota. This is the one remaining reason the server needs Supabase at
# all. The anon key is publishable by design, so the server falls back to the
# VITE_ values above when these are not set.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Per-account rate limits are applied after authentication, per fixed 60s window:
#   chat   20 requests / minute
#   vision   6 requests / minute
#   models  30 requests / minute
# Raise or lower them in server/ai/guard.ts (DEFAULT_LIMITS).

